  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The man is mapped as the entity that will achieve regime change through persistent effort",
  "description": "The text 'keep it up and you'll get some regime change' implies that the person depicted (the man) is the agent or representative of the political activism that will lead to regime change. The visual of the man, with his serious expression and prominent ring, is used to symbolize authority, determination, or leadership in the context of political change. The analogical mapping projects the textual concept of 'regime change' onto the visual entity of the man, suggesting he embodies the outcome or the force behind it. This is a classic propagandistic technique where a visual figure is associated with a desired political outcome.",
